@page "/help"
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Help · GymStation</PageTitle>

<main class="legal-shell">
    <header>
        <a class="legal-home" href="/"><BrandMark Size="1.5rem" />GYMSTATION</a>
        <h1>HELP</h1>
        <p class="legal-date">THE SHORT VERSION OF HOW EVERYTHING WORKS</p>
    </header>

    <h2>SIGNING IN</h2>
    <p>One login covers every gym you train at. If you belong to several, you'll pick
        which gym to open after signing in; if just one, you land straight in it. Your
        gym creates your login — if you don't have one, ask the front desk.</p>

    <h2>FOR MEMBERS</h2>
    <p><b>Schedule</b> shows your gym's week. Filter by class type or instructor, and
        check in from your phone once the check-in window opens (shortly before class —
        your gym sets how early). Forgot? Instructors can add you to the roll.</p>
    <p><b>Diary</b> is your private training log — what you drilled, who you rolled
        with, how it went. Staff can never read it.</p>
    <p><b>Progress</b> tracks your belt and stripe history, attendance stats, and your
        contact details, including whether your gym may text you.</p>
    <p><b>Events</b> lists tournaments, seminars, and gym happenings. RSVP so your gym
        can plan numbers.</p>
    <p>The bell in the top bar collects your notifications — class changes,
        cancellations, promotions, and event updates.</p>

    <h2>FOR INSTRUCTORS</h2>
    <p>The TEACH tab holds your classes: approve pending check-ins, add walk-ins to the
        roll, and request or claim substitutions when someone can't make their slot.</p>

    <h2>FOR GYM STAFF</h2>
    <p>The admin portal runs the gym: TODAY for the live roll, ROSTER for people,
        RANKS for promotions, SCHEDULE for templates and one-off changes, DUES for the
        monthly cycle and arrears, EVENTS for publishing, REPORTS for the numbers, and
        SETTINGS for branding, class tags, and workflow options.</p>

    <h2>WHEN SOMETHING'S WRONG</h2>
    <p>Account, membership, or billing questions: talk to your gym's staff — they own
        those records. Gym owners with a platform problem can reach the operator through
        their usual channel.</p>

    <PlatformFooter />
</main>
